\"All experience and education start/end fields are native input[type=month] (consistent month/year entry); preview renders them consistently as \\\"Mar 2017 - Dec 2019\\\", \\\"Jan 2020 - Jun 2022\\\", education \\\"Sep 2013 - Jun 2016\\\". Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" cleared the end date (value \\\"\\\") and set disabled=true; preview switched to \\\"Jan 2020 - Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all resume changes are lost on reload and deletions are resurrected\", \"actual\": \"Before reload the dashboard held 4 resumes: \\\"ML Engineer Resume\\\" (duplicated + renamed + edited), \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\" (created new + fully authored + renamed + edited), \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\", \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\"; \\\"Product Designer Resume\\\" had been deleted via the confirm dialog. After reloading http://localhost:7005/ the dashboard reset to the 3 original seeded resumes (Product Designer, Marketing Manager, Software Engineer). Both newly created/duplicated resumes and every edit and rename were lost, and the deleted \\\"Product Designer Resume\\\" reappeared. localStorage and sessionStorage are both completely empty ({}), confirming state is held only in memory.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-reload dashboard.resumes items: resume-3 \\\"Product Designer Resume\\\" (Feb 25 2024), resume-2 \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\", resume-1 \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\". localStorageKeys=[], sessionStorageKeys=[].\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Dashboard rename dialog accepts whitespace-only title, blanking the resume name; no validation feedback on either rename path\", \"actual\": \"Two rename paths, both defective. (1) Dashboard card menu > Rename: entered \\\"   \\\" (whitespace-only) and clicked Save — the dialog closed and the rename was APPLIED. The card title is now empty (dashboard.resumes item name = \\\"\\\", card innerText = \\\"\\\"), so the resume is left with no visible title and no validation message or toast appeared. (2) Editor inline title: entering \\\"   \\\" or \\\"\\\" reverted to the previous title, which is correct, but produced no validation feedback (no toast, no [role=alert]/[role=status], nothing matching empty/required/cannot/invalid; polled ~720ms). Neither path gives the user clear validation feedback, and the dashboard path violates the requirement that the current title remains.\", \"evidence\": \"After saving \\\"   \\\" in the rename dialog: dashboard.resumes.item.ck1l84sbrnn name=\\\"\\\" while other cards keep their titles; toasts array empty.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Filling contact fields immediately produced matching preview observables (preview.contact.name \\\"Ada Lovelace\\\", email, phone, location, linkedin, website) with no save action. Summary and experience edits likewise appeared in preview.document instantly (\\\"Mar 2017 - Dec 2019\\\", \\\"Jan 2020 - Jun 2022\\\"). Template switching verified separately in FT-2.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Moving Education up immediately re-rendered preview.document with EDUCATION before WORK EXPERIENCE; toggling skills visibility off/on immediately removed/restored the SKILLS block — no save or refresh needed. After navigating to the dashboard and reopening the resume, the sections list still reads contact, summary, education, experience, skills with the new order intact and the preview still shows Academics before Career History.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All edits (contact, summary, experience, education, skills, template, section order/headings, title) were retained automatically with no explicit save while moving between editor tabs, navigating back to the dashboard via editor.back, and reopening the resume card. The dashboard card reflected the update: title \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\", \\\"Updated Aug 28, 2026\\\" (today) and template badge \\\"Minimal\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In Minimal (and verified in Modern/Classic) the preview rendered every visible section holding content: contact block, summary text, education entry, both experience entries with dates/descriptions, and both skills. Hidden sections are omitted (verified in FT-4). With viewport reduced to 1280x500 so the resume exceeded the visible area, the page scrolled (scrollHeight 998 > clientHeight 500) and scrolling to the bottom brought the final section into the viewport with the document bottom visible, so the complete resume stays readable. Note: the missing Minimal summary heading is recorded separately under CT-20.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After switching among Contact/Summary/Experience/Education/Skills/Template/Sections tabs, returning to the dashboard and reopening the resume: contact fields all retained (Ada Lovelace, ada@example.com, 555-0100, London, UK, linkedin.com/in/ada, ada.dev); summary text retained in full; both experience entries (Research Analyst @ Babbage Works Mar 2017–Dec 2019, Lead Programmer @ Analytical Engines Ltd Jan 2020–Jun 2022) with descriptions; education (University of London, BSc Mathematics, GPA 3.9, Sep 2013–Jun 2016); both skills (Mathematics, Algorithm Design).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Copy→original: after editing the copy (name \\\"Ada L. Byron\\\", email \\\"copy@example.com\\\", added skill \\\"Machine Learning\\\"), reopening the original still showed \\\"Ada Lovelace\\\", \\\"ada@example.com\\\" and no Machine Learning in its preview. Original→copy: after changing the original's location to \\\"Cambridge, UK\\\", reopening the copy still showed location \\\"London, UK\\\" with its own edits intact (title \\\"ML Engineer Resume\\\", \\\"Ada L. Byron\\\", \\\"copy@example.com\\\", Machine Learning present). Edits are fully isolated in both directions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed \\\"Untitled Resume\\\" → \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\" in the editor; editor.title observed as \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\". After navigating back, the dashboard card shows the same non-empty title \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized summary heading not rendered in the Minimal style\", \"actual\": \"Section headings were customized to: summary=\\\"About Me\\\", experience=\\\"Career History\\\", education=\\\"Academics\\\", skills=\\\"Core Competencies\\\". Modern preview shows all four (\\\"About Me\\\", \\\"Academics\\\", \\\"Career History\\\", \\\"Core Competencies\\\"); Classic shows all four (\\\"ABOUT ME\\\", \\\"ACADEMICS\\\", \\\"CAREER HISTORY\\\", \\\"CORE COMPETENCIES\\\"). Minimal renders \\\"ACADEMICS\\\", \\\"CAREER HISTORY\\\" and \\\"CORE COMPETENCIES\\\" but omits the summary heading entirely — the summary body text (\\\"Pioneering analytical engine programmer...\\\") appears with no heading above it even though the summary section is visible.\", \"evidence\": \"Minimal preview text: \\\"...ADA.DEV\\\\n\\\\nPioneering analytical engine programmer with a passion for mathematics.\\\\n\\\\nACADEMICS...\\\" — no \\\"About Me\\\" heading; regex /About Me/i on preview.document = false.\"}]}"
