    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 21 checklist items have been executed and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**16 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\nThe core resume-building experience is solid: creation, editing all content types (contact, summary, experience, education, skills), reordering and removing entries, all three templates, section reordering/visibility, preview toggling, duplication with full edit isolation, and case-insensitive search with newest/oldest sorting all work correctly. Live preview updates are instant, and in-session state survives tab switches and dashboard round trips.\n\n### Failures\n\n**FT-19 — Date filtering is entirely missing.** The dashboard offers only a search box and a sort dropdown. There is no date input, range control, or clear-date affordance anywhere, so the requirement cannot be met at all.\n\n**CS-11 — No persistence (most severe).** All state is in-memory only; `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` are empty. After a reload, the two resumes I created/duplicated vanished, every edit and rename was lost, and the resume I had deleted through its confirmation dialog reappeared. This undermines the product's central promise of saving multiple variations for different applications.\n\n**CS-21 — Whitespace rename corrupts data.** Two rename paths behave inconsistently. The editor's inline title correctly reverts an empty/whitespace entry, but the *dashboard rename dialog accepts* `\"   \"` and applies it, leaving the card with a completely blank title. Neither path shows any validation feedback.\n\n**CS-9 — No date-period validation.** An end month preceding the start month (2020-01 → 2019-05) and fully future periods (2030-03 → 2031-09) are both accepted silently on experience *and* education entries, with no error text, no `aria-invalid`, and no `max` constraint on the inputs.\n\n**CT-20 — Custom heading dropped in Minimal.** The customized summary heading (\"About Me\") renders in Modern and Classic but is omitted entirely in the Minimal style, even though the summary section is visible and its body text renders. The other three custom headings appear correctly in all styles, so this is isolated to the Minimal template's summary block.\n\nTwo notes on judgment calls: I passed CT-15 because every visible section with content does render and the full resume stays reachable by scrolling (verified at a reduced 1280×500 viewport) — the Minimal heading gap is tracked under CT-20 rather than double-counted. I also confirmed FT-8's sort follows *creation* order rather than update order, since the duplicated resume sorted newest despite the original having been edited more recently."
  }
}
